{"archetypes":[{"name":"git-commit-flag-contract","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's scoped-commit fix depends on git-commit.sh supporting --only and --pathspec-from-file flags that may not exist; if absent the fix silently fails to exclude carryover from round commits.","prompt_body":"The plan proposes replacing unscoped git-commit.sh calls with `git-commit.sh --only --pathspec-from-file \"$stage_manifest\"` for both primary and follow-up round commits (plan items 5 and 6). Verify that `scripts/git-commit.sh` actually accepts `--only` and `--pathspec-from-file` as recognized flags by reading its source; if either flag is absent or handled differently than the plan assumes, the scoped-commit fix will not prevent outside-manifest carryover from entering round commits. Also check whether `git-commit.sh` performs its own `git add` before `git commit --only` — the plan claims it \"already stages from the pathspec file before `git commit --only --pathspec-from-file=…`\"; if the script does not stage from the pathspec file before committing, the `--only` flag alone will not exclude pre-staged carryover paths. Cross-check the actual `git-commit.sh` implementation against all flag-contract assumptions the plan relies on without quoting the file. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sed-extract-dependency","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Test case A sed-extracts multiple shell helpers for isolated unit testing; any unextracted transitive dependency or sed boundary mismatch will cause the test to error rather than assert.","prompt_body":"The plan's test case A instructs the implementer to sed-extract `pre_coder_path_diff_file`, `capture_round_tracked_paths`, `path_is_pre_coder_carryover`, and `round_tracked_dirty_outside_manifest` from `review-and-fix.sh` and define a `larch_err` stub. Read `review-and-fix.sh` and `test-review-and-fix.sh` to verify: (1) `path_is_pre_coder_carryover` does not call any helper beyond `pre_coder_path_diff_file` that also needs extraction; (2) `capture_round_tracked_paths` has no undeclared dependencies that break in an extracted context; (3) the existing sed range or pattern boundaries used to extract `round_tracked_dirty_outside_manifest` (plan references lines ~463-480) will still capture the full extended function body after the function gains a second optional argument — a boundary anchored on the old closing brace or line count would silently truncate the new code. Flag any missing extraction dependency or sed boundary mismatch that would cause the test to exit with a shell error rather than produce a meaningful assertion failure. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-repurpose-adequacy","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan repurposes manifest-outside-orchestrator by swapping its TEST_AGENT_BEHAVIOR stub but specifies the new stub only in prose, leaving unaddressed whether existing case-block emission contracts and assertion bodies must also change.","prompt_body":"The plan repurposes the existing `manifest-outside-orchestrator` test case (lines ~482-501) by introducing `TEST_AGENT_BEHAVIOR=outside-manifest-break-carryover` — a stub that mimics `codex-success` but also appends to `other.txt` during dispatch. Read `test-review-and-fix.sh` to verify: (1) what each `TEST_AGENT_BEHAVIOR` stub must write or emit (manifest file, exit-code file, or other sentinel) to satisfy `review-and-fix.sh`'s post-dispatch coder-output contract — the new stub must satisfy the same contract or dispatch will fail for the wrong reason; (2) whether the append-to-`other.txt` mutation is detectable by the `cmp -s` snapshot check given the exact point at which `review-and-fix.sh` snapshots the file during dispatch; (3) whether the existing `manifest-outside-orchestrator` test body contains any substring assertions on stderr messages, `CODER_STATUS` env paths, or HEAD state that would need updating after the stub changes but are not called out in the plan. Any unaddressed case-block requirement or stale assertion is a plan gap the implementer will hit at test time. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
